# Markdown file naming (Porto SDK Lab)

## Rule

- **Always lowercase** file names.
- **One word:** `dependency.md`, `config.md`, `debugging.md`, `resources.md`.
- **Group with a subfolder** when topics share a prefix — do not use multi-word filenames (`docs/labs/resources.md`, not `local-resources.md`).
- **No `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`** or `PascalCase` in doc file names.

## Exceptions (repo conventions)

Keep standard GitHub root filenames as-is: `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `LICENSE`.

Architectural decisions live in one file: `docs/adr.md` (sections, not numbered files).

## Examples

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| `PORTO_STACK_ARCHITECTURE.md` | `docs/stack.md` |
| `PUBLIC_API.md` | `docs/sdks/public.md` |
| `SDK_ARCHITECTURE.md` | `docs/sdks/architecture.md` |
| `FEATURE_ANALYSIS.md` | removed — catalog mapping lives in porto-data |
| `DEBUGGING.md` | `labs/debugging.md` |
| `LOCAL_RESOURCE_PACKAGES_DEVELOPMENT.md` | `docs/labs/resources.md` |
| `known-gaps.md` | `docs/sdks/gaps.md` |

When adding or renaming docs, update all cross-links in the same change.
